INSTALL.readme — NitroWebExpress (NWE)
Java National Finance Engine v2811.1
MEARVK LLC — Author: Max Rupplin
========================================

REQUIREMENTS
------------
  - Linux (Ubuntu 22.04+ recommended)
  - Java 21 JDK          (javac and java on PATH)
  - sudo access          (for MySQL install only)
  - Internet access      (for apt package download)


QUICK START  (three commands)
------------------------------
  1.  bash bash/mysql-setup.sh        # install + configure MySQL
  2.  bash bash/nwe-install.sh        # compile source, stage classes, chmod scripts
  3.  bash scripts/startup.sh         # start NitroWebExpress


STEP 1 — MySQL
--------------
  bash bash/mysql-setup.sh

  What it does:
    - Checks sudo access (exits with a clear message if not available)
    - Installs mysql-server via apt  (skipped if already installed)
    - Enables and starts the MySQL service
    - Creates database N21 and user 'mearvk' with password from mysql.auth.xml
    - Runs scripts/N21.table.builder.sh to create all application tables
    - Writes authentication/mysql.auth.xml (chmod 600) if not already present

  Override the app-user password:
    bash bash/mysql-setup.sh --password MyNewPassword

  Sudo note:
    The script requires sudo for apt and mysql administration.
    If sudo is not available it will print a clear error and exit.
    Run as a user with sudo, or:
      sudo -E bash bash/mysql-setup.sh


STEP 2 — Build / Install
-------------------------
  bash bash/nwe-install.sh

  What it does:
    - Sets executable permission (chmod +x) on all .sh files in bash/ and scripts/
    - Compiles all source/*.java files to out/  (skips if classes are up-to-date)
    - Moves any stray .class files left in source/ to their correct path in out/

  Force a full recompile:
    bash bash/nwe-install.sh --force


STEP 3 — Start
--------------
  bash scripts/startup.sh

  Starts the JVM with G1GC, 512 MB min heap, 4 GB max heap, classpath out/.
  On startup NweConfig reads configuration/nwe-config.xml and enables/disables
  each service according to the <enabled> flags.


STOP
----
  bash scripts/shutdown.sh

  Sends SIGTERM then SIGKILL to any process bound to an NWE port.


CONFIGURATION
-------------
  configuration/nwe-config.xml     Enable/disable individual services; set ports.
  authentication/mysql.auth.xml    MySQL host, port, username, password.

  Admin login (ModuleInstallationService / ModuleLoaderDaemon TCP sessions):
    Username and password are set in the <admin> block of nwe-config.xml.
    Default: username=mearvk  password=n21admin
    Change the password in nwe-config.xml before first production use.


SERVICE PORTS (default)
-----------------------
  49152   NitroWebExpress main
   5512   AES 2.0 server
   7743   RSA server
   7744   DSA server
   6682   Bitcoin server
  49155   Connection status server
  49177   ASCII creator server
  49166   Module installation service
  49188   Module loader daemon
   2000   Strernary™ Directory Server
  20000   Strernary™ Inference Server
   9999   GrayPortRegistry™ (standard)
  10085   Gray85 Crème Registry™
  49152   Brarner.M.Alete™ (masquerade-routed)
  49201   JapanSignalServer™
  49202   RussiaSignalServer™
  49203   MexicoSignalServer™
  49204   GreeceInternationalSignalServer™


BMA SERVLET WEBSITE
-------------------
  cd modules/black/presidential/Brarner.M.Alete/install
  bash download-jars.sh          # fetch Jakarta Servlet 6.1, MySQL 8.3, Tomcat 11.0.2
  bash install.sh                # deploy locally + optional remote to name.com


CONNECTING (telnet / nc)
------------------------
  telnet localhost 49152          # main NWE prompt
  nc    localhost 49155           # status report
  nc    localhost 49166           # module installation service
  nc    localhost 49188           # module loader daemon


LOGS
----
  logging/exceptions.log          Runtime exception log.
  database/fallback/                    XML fallback records when MySQL is unavailable.
